# Sinfonia No. 5 in E-flat major, BWV 791 (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a tender, aria-like duet. The two upper voices imitate each
# other in dotted rhythms over a bass that plays like a continuo (a
# rising arpeggio, then two quarters, every bar). Like a slow movement
# from a trio sonata. This Mutopia edition is the plain version, with
# no written-out ornaments.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 50. Timings for 38 bars: Andras Schiff (clavichord,
# ECM) 2:08, about 53; Angela Hewitt 2:37, about 44; Glenn Gould 3:08,
# about 36. 50 sits between Schiff and Hewitt; without ornaments the
# chip line would drag if it went slower.
#
# Structure (my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   1-9    subject top 1.75, answer mid 2.75 (in Bb); cadence in Eb
#          bar 9.
#   9-17   cadence in C minor bar 13; entries mid 13.75, top 14.75;
#          cadence in Bb major bar 17.
#   17-29  top 17.75 (highest register of the piece), mid 18.75, to a
#          cadence in F minor bar 25; mid 25.75, top 26.75; cadence in
#          Ab major bar 29.
#   29-38  reprise: bars 30-37 repeat bars 1-8 with the upper voices
#          exchanged (bass identical); final cadence bar 38.

tempo 50
rit 2 0.7                 # bars 37-38: the final cadence
broaden 24 0.95           # bar 24: into the F minor cadence, the turning point

voice mid 0               # the two upper voices are equal partners
voice bottom 1            # the bass accompanies, a step back

dyn 1 mp                  # bars 1-16: the tender opening duet
dyn 17 mf                 # bars 17-28: middle section, high register, flat keys
dyn 29 p                  # bars 29-38: reprise, played as an echo of the opening

lead 1.75-2 top           # subject in the top
lead 2.75-3 mid           # answer in the middle
lead 13.75-14 mid         # middle entry after the C minor cadence
lead 14.75-15 top         # top entry
lead 17.75-18 top         # top entry, high, after the Bb cadence
lead 18.75-19 mid         # middle entry
lead 25.75-26 mid         # middle entry after the F minor cadence
lead 26.75-27 top         # top entry
lead 30.75-31 mid         # reprise: the subject now in the middle
